  "selection_rationale": "The advanced penalised-spline model has the lower precision-weighted maturity-grouped holdout RMSE (1.89bp vs 2.88bp for the bootstrap baseline, 34% lower; unweighted RMSE 2.95bp vs 3.67bp, median absolute error 1.09bp vs 2.24bp, n=110 held-out instruments). By type - bond: advanced 2.53bp vs baseline 3.56bp (weighted); deposit: advanced 1.08bp vs baseline 2.59bp (weighted); ois_swap: advanced 1.70bp vs baseline 2.60bp (weighted).",
  "holdout_method": "Maturity-grouped 5-fold cross-validation: instruments are grouped into tenor clusters (all quotes of the same tenor, and bonds maturing within 2% of each other, form one cluster); whole clusters are assigned round-robin in maturity order to folds so near-duplicate quotes never straddle train and test; the shortest and longest clusters always stay in the training set (extrapolation is not scored). Both models are refitted on every training fold. Errors are market-minus-model in yield-equivalent basis points (bond price errors divided by dollar duration). Instruments rejected by the full-data robust fit are not scored.",
